  "claim": "Alice or the Last Escapade is a 1977 film written and directed by Claude Chabrol, loosely based on a novel by the author of the poem \"Jabberwocky\".",
  "evidencia": "Page: Alice or the Last Escapade. Sentence: Alice or the Last Escapade (French: \"Alice ou la dernière fugue\" ) is a 1977 film written and directed by Claude Chabrol.\nPage: Alice or the Last Escapade. Sentence: The film is very loosely inspired by \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\" by Lewis Carroll, including the protagonist's name being Alice Carroll (a combination of the Alice character and the author's pseudonymous surname).\nPage: Lewis Carroll. Sentence: His most famous writings are \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\", its sequel \"Through the Looking-Glass\", which includes the poem \"Jabberwocky\", and the poem \"The Hunting of the Snark\", all examples of the genre of literary nonsense.",
