        "original_id": "c19c8b9e-3f9e-5b40-a9c3-a54c1f118931",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Claude Chabrol, Lewis Carroll, Alice Carroll\n- Works: Alice or the Last Escapade, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, Through the Looking-Glass, Jabberwocky, The Hunting of the Snark\n- Concepts: literary nonsense, adaptation inspiration\n\nFacts:\n- In 1977, Claude Chabrol wrote and directed the film Alice or the Last Escapade.\n- Alice or the Last Escapade is very loosely inspired by Alice's Adventures in Wonderland by Lewis Carroll.\n- The protagonist of Alice or the Last Escapade is named Alice Carroll, combining the Alice character with Lewis Carroll's pseudonymous surname.\n- Lewis Carroll's most famous writings include Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, its sequel Through the Looking-Glass, the poem Jabberwocky included in Through the Looking-Glass, and the poem The Hunting of the Snark.\n- Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, Through the Looking-Glass, Jabberwocky, and The Hunting of the Snark are examples of literary nonsense.",
